 "_meta": {
  "description": "Single source of truth for crop water characteristics.",
  "why": "The frontend previously held TWO conflicting copies of this data (WaterRiskModal.jsx said wheat=3.4 mm/day, CropIntelligence.jsx said 4.2). This file replaces both.",
  "provenance": "referenceWaterDemandMmPerDay values are PROVISIONAL seed values carried over from the original UI mockup. They are flagged provisional:true and must be replaced by computed FAO-56 values (ETo x Kc) once the weather integration lands. Do not present them as authoritative.",
  "kcSource": "FAO Irrigation and Drainage Paper 56, Table 12 (single crop coefficients)",
  "stageModel": "stageFractions are the FAO-56 Table 11 stage lengths (kept verbatim in stageSourceDays) expressed as fractions of the season, so they always sum to growthDays exactly. The Kc curve is: Kc=kc.initial through the initial stage; a straight line from kc.initial to kc.mid across development; Kc=kc.mid through mid-season; a straight line from kc.mid to kc.late across the late stage (FAO-56 calls that last value Kc_end).",
  "stageCaveat": "Stage lengths and typicalSowing are generic FAO-56 / Haryana-calendar values, NOT field-verified for Haryana. An agronomist should review them before these numbers inform policy. growthDays was left at its existing value, so stage days are scaled to it rather than to the Table 11 totals.",
  "sowingCaveat": "typicalSowing is a single representative date per crop (MM-DD). Real sowing spreads over weeks and varies by district and monsoon onset."
 },
